{"slug": "digital-logic-gates-explained", "question": "What Are the 7 Basic Logic Gates?", "body_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Digital logic gates are <strong>circuits with one or more binary inputs and one output set by a fixed logical rule</strong>. The seven basic gates are AND, OR, NOT, NAND, NOR, XOR and XNOR.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0 4px;font-size:16px;\"><tr style=\"background:#1a2b4a;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Gate</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Output is 1 when</th></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">AND</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">All inputs are 1</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">OR</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Any input is 1</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">NOT</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Input is 0</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">NAND / NOR</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Inverse of AND / OR (universal gates)</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">XOR</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Inputs differ</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">XNOR</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Inputs match</td></tr></table>"}